            choice("brainteasers-induction", "challenge", "Mathematical induction", "Connect n to n + 1", "You know 1 + … + n = n(n+1)/2. Which expression completes the induction step after adding n+1?", [("a", "n(n+1)/2 + (n+1) = (n+1)(n+2)/2"), ("b", "n(n+1)/2 + (n+1) = n(n+2)/2"), ("c", "n(n+1)/2 + (n+1) = (n+1)²/2"), ("d", "Checking n = 2 proves every n.")], "a", ["Factor out n + 1.", "The expression left inside the brackets is n/2 + 1."], "The induction step must produce exactly the claimed formula with n replaced by n+1. Together with a valid base case, this proves the identity for positive integers.", ["Check the base case n = 1.", "Assume the formula holds for n.", "Add n+1 and factor to obtain (n+1)(n+2)/2."], "An induction proof needs both the starting case and a valid transition."),
